{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RvwhA8piqbM2opyjvQGGtp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers of Dream simulation scenarios.\n\nKey facts from the data:\n- exp029 episode-level: step15 val_success = 28.125%, pass_at_8 = 92.9%, train_success = 43.75%\n- exp028c step-independent: step10 val = 0% (catastrophic collapse)\n- hsweep_h2_seed1: collapse onset step3→step4, step9 success = 0%\n- Self-Guide baseline: 72.7% (1.7B)\n\n\n- GAGPO: 93.5% (1.5B)\n- HiPER: 97.4% (7B)\n\nI'm seeing the episode-level approach plateauing around 25-28% validation success, while step-independent training completely fails. The key question is whether episode-level can break through this plateau, and I need to verify whether the multi-seed results stay consistent and if the GAE baseline comparison actually supports what I'm trying to show. I'm also uncertain whether selective verification in Phase B is even feasible, and whether action-change as an intrinsic reward signal for verification will actually work in practice.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the outcome scenarios. Best case would be episode-level hitting 45%+ with stable multi-seed results, clean verification of the sign misattribution mechanism, and selective verification cutting costs by 40% with minimal performance loss—that's a full dual contribution paper. More realistically, episode-level might plateau somewhere between 30-40%, the mechanism analysis could be clean but selective verification only partially works or shows larger gaps, which would shift the paper toward a stronger diagnostic contribution. Worst case is if episode-level stays stuck around 28% or even regresses, multi-seed shows high variance, and the mechanism analysis gets noisy—then I'd need to reframe this as a pure diagnostic paper.\n\nI need to track several key metrics to evaluate which scenario we're in: episode-level validation success to see convergence, multi-seed standard deviation for stability, the correlation between sign misattribution and actual outcomes, how robust the mechanism is across hyperparameter sweeps, whether selective verification actually reduces costs while maintaining performance, and how the GAE comparison supports the overall narrative. I should make sure the numeric thresholds for best/median/worst are properly ordered.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20713,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20713},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c1c4090-aa63-458a-acac-30cd6ed54230","uuid":"1a8c2dc2-19f0-495d-8dfa-224a82bf932e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RvwhA8piqbM2opyjvQGGtp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level 持续收敛至强 baseline 水平，双机制理论被干净验证，selective verification 完整 story 成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - episode-level val_success 突破当前 28% plateau，收敛至 ≥45%\n      - multi-seed std < 5pp，结果可复现\n      - sign_misattribution 实证：sign-outcome correlation > 0.95，sign-local_quality correlation < 0.1\n      - h-sweep 在 3 seeds 下均展示 monotonic cliff，cliff 位置一致（h ≤ 5 崩溃）\n      - GAE baseline 与 episode-level GRPO 持平或略优（不大幅碾压，支持 \"episode-level 信息是关键\" 叙事）\n      - selective verification 训练收敛，action-change reward 有效\n      - B-IAVR 达成 verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_val_success_converged: [0.45, 0.60]\n      multi_seed_std: [0.02, 0.05]\n      sign_vs_outcome_correlation: [0.95, 1.0]\n      sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: [0.0, 0.1]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [5, 10]  # h 值低于此阈值时崩溃\n      GAE_vs_episode_delta: [-0.05, 0.05]  # GAE - episode_level，接近零\n      selective_verification_cost_reduction: [0.40, 0.60]\n      selective_success_delta_vs_always_on: [0.0, 0.03]  # 损失，越小越好\n      action_change_rate_confirmatory: [0.60, 0.80]  # 确认性验证占比\n      ScienceWorld_episode_vs_step_ratio: [2.0, 5.0]  # episode-level 倍数优势\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 dual contribution framing 完全成立。Paper = 诊断（sign misattribution 机制 + h-sweep cliff）\n      + 修复（episode-level GRPO）+ 应用（selective verification 降本）。\n      Contrarian solution story 强：社区走 finer credit，我们用 coarser 消除 misattribution，\n      且 GAE 对比证明 episode-level 信息而非 per-token credit 是关键。\n      Claims 1-3 全部 strong，NeurIPS/ICLR main track 可冲。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level 收敛但未达强 baseline，机制分析干净，selective verification 部分成立或效果打折\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - episode-level val_success 收敛至 30-44%，突破 plateau 但距 Self-Guide 72.7% 仍有显著差距\n      - multi-seed std 5-8pp，可复现但方差较大\n      - sign_misattribution 实证方向正确但不完全干净（correlation 0.8-0.95，存在噪声）\n      - h-sweep cliff 存在但 3 seeds 中 1 seed 表现异常（cliff 位置不完全一致）\n      - GAE baseline 显著优于 episode-level GRPO（+8-15pp），削弱 \"coarser suffices\" 的叙事\n      - selective verification 可训练但效果打折：cost reduction 20-39% 或 success delta 3-8pp\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_val_success_converged: [0.30, 0.44]\n      multi_seed_std: [0.05, 0.08]\n      sign_vs_outcome_correlation: [0.80, 0.95]\n      sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: [0.1, 0.25]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [3, 5]\n      GAE_vs_episode_delta: [0.08, 0.15]  # GAE 显著更好\n      selective_verification_cost_reduction: [0.20, 0.39]\n      selective_success_delta_vs_always_on: [0.03, 0.08]\n      action_change_rate_confirmatory: [0.50, 0.65]\n      ScienceWorld_episode_vs_step_ratio: [1.3, 2.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要调整 claims 强度。Claim 1 仍 strong（diagnostic contribution 稳固），但 contrarian story 需弱化：\n      如果 GAE >> episode-level，则 \"coarser suffices\" 变为 \"coarser is necessary but not sufficient，\n      episode-level 消除 misattribution 但仍需更好 credit\"。\n      Claim 2/3 降为 preliminary：selective verification 作为 proof-of-concept 而非成熟系统。\n      Paper 重心移向诊断贡献（占 60%+），selective verification 作为下游应用 demo。\n      Self-Guide 3x gap 需正面讨论（不同 paradigm，不 claim performance parity）。\n      EMNLP/NeurIPS workshop → main track 需看最终数字。补充 GAE 深度分析 + community practice survey。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level plateau 未突破或回退，机制分析有噪声，selective verification 无法进行\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - episode-level val_success 停滞在 25-30% 或回退（与当前 step15=28.1% 无实质提升）\n      - multi-seed 中 ≥2/5 seeds 未收敛或崩溃，std > 8pp，结果不稳定\n      - sign_misattribution 方向正确但 correlation < 0.8，审稿人可质疑因果性\n      - h-sweep cliff 不 monotonic（中间 h 值反而更差），削弱理论预测\n      - GAE baseline 大幅碾压（+20pp+），episode-level GRPO 看起来只是 \"less bad\" 而非 solution\n      - val_success < 40% 导致 selective verification 无意义（Claim 2/3 放弃）\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_val_success_converged: [0.25, 0.30]\n      multi_seed_std: [0.08, 0.15]\n      sign_vs_outcome_correlation: [0.60, 0.80]\n      sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: [0.2, 0.4]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [2, 3]\n      GAE_vs_episode_delta: [0.15, 0.30]\n      selective_verification_cost_reduction: null  # 不执行\n      selective_success_delta_vs_always_on: null\n      action_change_rate_confirmatory: null\n      ScienceWorld_episode_vs_step_ratio: [1.0, 1.3]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心 reframe：放弃 dual contribution，转为纯诊断 paper（Plan A）。\n      新 angle = \"Why Step-Independent RL Fails for LLM Agents: A Mechanistic Autopsy\"。\n      贡献变为：(1) 首次系统量化 step-independent 的双机制失效（即使 correlation 不完美，\n      趋势方向正确 + 代码级 root cause 分析仍有价值），(2) h-sweep 作为实践指南\n      （\"多大 h 才安全\"），(3) 对 RAGEN/社区框架的 actionable 修复建议，\n      (4) 与 Turn-PPO/GAGPO 的理论统一（sign misattribution 作为 uniform advantage 的泛化）。\n      不 claim solution，claim diagnosis depth。需要大幅加深分析：\n      gradient flow 可视化、per-token advantage heatmap、failure mode taxonomy。\n      如果 GAE 碾压，反而可加入：\"episode-level GRPO 消除 misattribution 但仍缺 fine credit，\n      two orthogonal failure modes need two fixes\"。不降 venue，但定位从 method paper 变为 analysis paper。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20713,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20713},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c1c4090-aa63-458a-acac-30cd6ed54230","uuid":"cf2893f1-c432-4d94-a50e-6dd49a42b65e"}
